    "tags": [],
    "description": {
      "value": "<p><strong>Fractal Self.</strong> You briefly exist across multiple symbolic frames, slipping between potential versions of yourself.</p><p><strong>Once per Soma Break</strong>, when you take an action, you may manifest a Fractal Afterimage:</p><ul><li>Teleport up to <strong>2 squares</strong> to an unoccupied space you can see.</li><li>Gain <strong>advantage</strong> on the next attack roll, skill check, or defense check you make within 1 minute.</li><li>Until the start of your next turn, <strong>attacks roll 3d10 keep lowest 2</strong> against you.</li></ul><p>Bad Eden systems may treat this state as a nonlinear presence in Travel, Encounter, and Spark metaphysics.</p>",
      "chat": ""
    },
